    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d355">

                <pb facs="0600" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.2/7—3054: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Matthews</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-07-30T19:00:00+01:00">July 30, 1954—7
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>181. Secretary General Foreign Office tells me eighteen countries now firmly
                    committed themselves to support Van Kleffens. List includes five Latin American,
                    and two Asian countries and several Commonwealth dominions. In addition number
                    of others have indicated probable support but are not formally committed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matthews</hi>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
